    "created_at": "2026-08-06T02:51:43Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-08-06T02:51:43Z",
    "body": "> Thanks for the report, I'll look into it and try fixing the migration files. It's strange that this wasn't caught because we have a test to apply these migrations.\n\nThat pretty much sums up my entire existence; I'm always the one and only to have even the most obscure bug rear its head as soon as I go to use it (any app or product).\n\n> Honestly I would recommend just using the built in SQLite version in the meantime, less configuration and much better performance. We might remove support for MySQL entirely in the future as there are less than 10 users of it\n\nI personally tend to prefer either mysql or postgres over sqlite, especially in a swarm, because I can keep all of my apps' DBs in one nice, tidy UI (ie phpadmin) and don't have to mess around with using other apps to keep the db in sync across nodes (ie setting up something like syncthing to watch for changes).\n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
